  "id": "COMPOUND:36014 - PROTEIN:1107",
  "verbalization": "Jasplakinolide Z1 is shown to have a target relationship with Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf through multiple pathways, with the drug acting as a target for several different proteins, including integrin alpha-4, isoleucine--tRNA ligase, and ephrin type-B receptor 4. These proteins are all identified as targets of specific compounds, which in turn are linked to Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf. The evidence suggests that Jasplakinolide Z1 may exert its biological effects by modulating the activity of these downstream targets, which are involved in various cellular processes. The shared involvement of Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf across these pathways implies a potential role in the regulation of these targets, possibly through a common signaling mechanism or a direct interaction with the kinase. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Jasplakinolide Z1 may influence cellular functions by targeting a network of proteins that ultimately converge on Serine/threonine-protein kinase B-raf, highlighting a possible role in cellular signaling or homeostasis.",
